---
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/notes-app-block-write-light.svg?raw';
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/notes-app-block-write-dark.svg?raw';
import Chart from './Chart.astro';
---

<Chart
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  title="One of five states makes the writer back off"
  caption="What a guarded writer does with a fenced block, by what it finds on the page."
>
  Five states a writer can find and what it does with each. No block on the page yet: insert it and stamp the hash. An
  opening marker with no closing marker: write nothing. A marker that carries no hash, from an older block: replace the
  body and stamp it now. A stamped hash that matches the body on disk: replace and restamp. A stamped hash that differs
  because I edited inside the fence: skip, and my edit stays. A force flag overrides the skip.
</Chart>
